=== build note: no git history ===
rebuilding localhost/sextile:local (no git history, so every start checks for changes)
[exit 0]

=== build note: uncommitted changes ===
rebuilding localhost/sextile:v0.1.0-rc.1-dirty (uncommitted changes)
[exit 0]

=== busy port ===
port 5307 is in use. Run sextile --port 5308
[exit 2]

=== no terminal, no folder chosen ===
no charts folder is chosen and there is no terminal to ask. Run sextile --charts-dir DIR
[exit 2]

=== remote endpoint ===
only a local Docker is supported (this endpoint is tcp://build-host:2375): Sextile mounts a folder of this machine, which a remote Docker cannot see
[exit 2]

=== config: relative XDG_CONFIG_HOME ===
XDG_CONFIG_HOME is not an absolute path (relative/cfg). Set it to one or unset it
[exit 2]

=== config: inside the clone ===
the config location $CLONE/cfg/sextile/launcher.conf is inside the Sextile checkout ($CLONE). Set XDG_CONFIG_HOME to a folder outside it
[exit 2]

=== config: folder is a symlink ===
the config folder $XDG/sextile is a symlink. The launcher will not read or write through it
[exit 2]

=== config: not valid ===
the config file $XDG/sextile/launcher.conf is not valid: it must hold exactly one line, charts-dir=<absolute folder>. Fix it or delete it to be asked again
[exit 2]

=== config: remembered folder is gone ===
the remembered charts folder $TMP/usb/charts (from $XDG/sextile/launcher.conf) does not exist — Sextile will not create it again, in case a disk is not mounted. Restore it, fix the file, or delete the file to be asked again
[exit 2]

=== docker: permission denied ===
you cannot reach the Docker daemon (permission denied on its socket). Join the docker group (https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/linux-postinstall/) or start Docker Desktop
[exit 2]

=== forwarded --charts-dir ===
--charts-dir=/elsewhere would override the charts folder this launcher mounts. Use sextile --charts-dir DIR (before any --)
[exit 2]

=== --no-docker: go absent ===
--no-docker did not find go. It needs go (Go 1.25 or newer) on PATH, and astrolog on PATH or in ~/.local/bin (scripts/build-astrolog installs Astrolog, about two minutes)
[exit 2]

=== --no-docker: go and astrolog absent ===
--no-docker did not find go and astrolog. It needs go (Go 1.25 or newer) on PATH, and astrolog on PATH or in ~/.local/bin (scripts/build-astrolog installs Astrolog, about two minutes)
[exit 2]

=== --no-docker: the build fails ===
fake go: build failed
the native build failed (exit 3) — Sextile was not started
[exit 3]

=== --no-docker: no git history ===
native build of local (no git history, so every start rebuilds)
[exit 0]

